      "identification": "Unsigned native x64 resource crypter / reflective PE loader with forged Windows Update Assistant branding; no established malware-family attribution.",
      "evidence": [
        "Version fields claim Microsoft Corporation / Windows Update Assistant, original filename windows_update_assistant.exe and internal name msedgeupdate; no Authenticode record exists; PE timestamp is 2043.",
        "Entry 0x140003900 calls 0x1400032d0. Main reads its own file and path, computes a modified FNV-1a fingerprint, uses a hex fingerprint value under HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer as a DWORD execution marker. This is execution-state storage, not an autorun registration.",
        "Main reconstructs GetTickCount/GetTickCount64 and resource APIs in stack buffers and resolves them. It waits for uptime exceeding 30 minutes and last input within 10 minutes, pumping messages and sleeping 120 seconds between checks. YUKON_FORCE=1 bypasses these gates.",
        "Worker at 0x140001470 concatenates numbered BIN resources, derives a shuffled Base85 alphabet and inverse byte substitution table, decodes Base85 groups, applies a generated XOR keystream, then expands a custom LZ history-copy stream.",
        "An inert Unicorn API shim recovered a 2242048-byte x64 PE, SHA256 e628c30af922c6cd54b2e946960af3aa6088dcac2f713449002325bf77b295fe. No native sample instructions were executed by the host OS.",
        "Loader validates MZ/PE headers, copies sections to allocated memory, handles relocations, imports and TLS callbacks, assigns section protections and registers unwind metadata via RtlAddFunctionTable. CreateThread receives a wrapper that calls mapped base plus entry-point offset. Emulation stopped before that thread executed.",
        "Intermediate buffers are overwritten with zero bytes before VirtualFree/HeapFree. The YAML zero-fill and decompression patterns match original instructions, not inferred sandbox-only actions.",
        "Separate bounded emulation of the inner entry performed initialization then stopped at its first unmapped PEB access (0x14000c21a). Modified data contained a global mutex name, PING, a HELLO record with v3.1F, qemu-ga, and a Steam profile URL. These are recovered configuration leads; final command dispatch has not been established.",
        "The combined forged branding, delayed/user-input gating, custom concealed executable and manual image activation tips the verdict. Who deployed it and its final operational task are unknown."
      ],
